WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.353
Another network model you need to know about for the exam is the Transmission Control Protocol, or TCP model.

00:06.353 --> 00:18.117
Whereas the OSI model has seven layers, the TCP model has just four layers: Data-link, Network or Internet, Transport, and Application.

00:18.117 --> 00:29.524
The four layers of the TCP model map to the seven layers of the OSI model as follows: Physical and Data-link on OSI to Data-link on TCP;

00:29.524 --> 00:44.512
Network on OSI to Network or Internet on TCP; Transport layer on OSI to Transport layer on TCP; and the Session, Presentation, and Application layers on OSI to Application on TCP.

00:44.512 --> 00:51.612
The key takeaway for the exam is that the top layer of the TCP model covers the top three layers of the OSI model,

00:51.612 --> 00:57.559
and that the bottom layer of the TCP model covers the bottom two layers of the OSI model.

